  "configuration_id": "config_009",
  "reason": "1) Evidence/uncertainty: No experiments have been completed, so there is no performance baseline. We do not yet know how well a simple single-modality, single-profile model performs, which is essential for judging whether multimodal integration, multiprofile aggregation, or more complex encoders actually add value. 2) What this tests: config_009 (rna_only, singleprofile, scvi_n200, no aggregation, no fusion) is the simplest possible pipeline in the search space. It isolates the performance of the scvi_n200 RNA representation on a single profile with no confounding factors from image modality, aggregation, or fusion. 3) Why it is the best first experiment: Establishing a clean performance floor is the highest-information first step under a limited budget. Without it, any later multimodal or multiprofile result is ambiguous—we cannot tell if gains come from added complexity or if the baseline was already near ceiling. This single experiment reduces uncertainty about the most fundamental question (does the data support good classification at all?) and provides a reference against which every subsequent design axis (modality, profile, encoder, aggregation, fusion) can be evaluated with controlled comparisons."
}

